  "details": "After a world sets the player's height using SetAvatarEyeHeightByMeters(), running VRChat calibration does not preserve the value.\n\nWhen calibration is executed, the height set by the world is ignored and reverts to the last height value configured in the VRChat menu.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. In a world, set the player's height using SetAvatarEyeHeightByMeters().\n\n2. Run VRChat's calibration.\n\n3. The height set by the world is lost and changes back to the last height set in the VRChat menu.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nRunning calibration should not cause the height set via SetAvatarEyeHeightByMeters() to revert to the height value configured in the VRChat menu.",
